{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1496197-updating-transylvania-chronicles-to-later-edition","id":1496197,"title":"Updating Transylvania Chronicles to later edition","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-11-04T08:59:45-07:00","id":1496197,"title":"Updating Transylvania Chronicles to later edition","content":"So, in the latest episode of my podcast (cheeky little plug <a href=\"https://wodarkages.squarespace.com/podcast/interview-with-a-vampire-storyteller\" target=\"_blank\">https://wodarkages.squarespace.com/p...re-storyteller</a> ), I got to talking about the idea of updating Transylvania Chronicles to a later edition of the game. The inspiration is the update of Warhammer's famous Enewmy Within campaign to the 4th edition of WFRP.<br /> <br /> So, it'd have to be 20th Anniversary Edition, since 5e doesn't have a Dark Ages version.<br /> <br /> Do you think it could be done? Do you think people would be interested? Can it be updated without it being changing so much it becomes way too different?<br /> What do you think?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Freelance Writer and Storyteller's Vault contributor. Find my work here: <a href=\"http://www.storytellersvault.com/index.php?affiliate_id=17903\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.storytellersvault.com/ind...liate_id=17903</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1535-jackob","name":"Jackob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1535_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-04T09:09:36-07:00","id":1496198,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jackob</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1496197-updating-transylvania-chronicles-to-later-edition#post1496197\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, in the latest episode of my podcast (cheeky little plug <a href=\"https://wodarkages.squarespace.com/podcast/interview-with-a-vampire-storyteller\" target=\"_blank\">https://wodarkages.squarespace.com/p...re-storyteller</a> ), I got to talking about the idea of updating Transylvania Chronicles to a later edition of the game. The inspiration is the update of Warhammer's famous Enewmy Within campaign to the 4th edition of WFRP.<br /> <br /> So, it'd have to be 20th Anniversary Edition, since 5e doesn't have a Dark Ages version.<br /> <br /> Do you think it could be done? Do you think people would be interested? Can it be updated without it being changing so much it becomes way too different?<br /> What do you think?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Well, it has been ages since i've given Transylvania Chronicles a good, long read and currently more familiar with V20 than DAV20 proper, so my idea of how DA updates and events since TC came out might affect or clash with the series (except for the possibility of Tremere possessing Goratrix in the middle ages already and the Wan Kuei being erased from continuity) is vague overall, but I definitely think it can be done.<br /> <br /> Big matter, imho at least, is actually getting a clearer and more focused idea of what Transylvania Chronicles is really about, because the original books were quite scattershot with their info and never settled on what the PCs were struggling with from what i remember. Had some serious murky schizo plot issues worthy of <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=4tk664MfQgU\" target=\"_blank\">Lost</a>, if memory tricks me not.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 11-04-2022, 12:26 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-04T12:36:39-07:00","id":1496215,"title":"","content":"Do I think it could be done? Yeah, I don't see why not, probably take a bit to convert over, but it should be pretty smooth. Do I think people would be interested? Now that is an interesting question. In my opinion the problem with Transylvania Chronicles isn't the edition but the fact that so much of the Chronicle just isn't <i>fun</i> to play through. A lot of those older DA Chronicles just are like set pieces to get to modern rather than a game to play in, at least from my experience in both playing and running them.<br /> <br /> So, the question of 'Can it be updated without it being changing so much it becomes way too different?' I think they <i>should</i> be updated to the point of changing a lot to make it into something that is more involved with the players and doesn't feel like they are playing second to the NPCs.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12895-mrnatas","name":"MrNatas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12895_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"180"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-04T13:20:49-07:00","id":1496218,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrNatas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1496197-updating-transylvania-chronicles-to-later-edition?p=1496215#post1496215\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do I think it could be done? Yeah, I don't see why not, probably take a bit to convert over, but it should be pretty smooth. Do I think people would be interested? Now that is an interesting question. In my opinion the problem with Transylvania Chronicles isn't the edition but the fact that so much of the Chronicle just isn't <i>fun</i> to play through. A lot of those older DA Chronicles just are like set pieces to get to modern rather than a game to play in, at least from my experience in both playing and running them.</div> </div> </div> </div>I can't say i see things quite the same way, but it's true that TC as written, specially in the first two books, involves a lot of railroad &quot;thou shall not change setting event X&quot; in its main chapters, mixed with little to no guidance to the ST in blending the threads in these chapters into its own chronicle of the intervening decades or centuries between them.<br /> <br /> Going by book as written &quot;play through this event, skip/power up a century or two, play another unavoidable event with little setup, rinse, repeat&quot; seems indeed like very <b>easy</b> to fall into, i'll agree on that.<br /> <br /> Truth be told i'm partly curious because to this day i'm not 100% sure of what Transylvania Chronicles plot is even supposed to be in the first place - imprisoning Kupala? The Tzimisce antediluvian relocating its consciousness/soul into the Cathedral of Flesh? Saulot secretly being a psycho that created the Baali because he got pissed with Caine not being really the first vampire as he told them and the Wan Kuei already existed (what as an aside is not canon anymore)? The Nosferatu antediluvian tricking the Tremere &amp; Tzimisce through Zelios into setting up for it a demon-powered geomantic hack of cold war era silos that it would command into doing a nuclear missile volley on the Eldest in New York? All of those together and more somehow?<br /> <br /> Honestly, no idea whatsoever and seeing an update attempt should be fun to discuss for varied perspectives and try to make sense of that seeming trainwreck at least.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrNatas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1496197-updating-transylvania-chronicles-to-later-edition?p=1496215#post1496215\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, the question of 'Can it be updated without it being changing so much it becomes way too different?' I think they <i>should</i> be updated to the point of changing a lot to make it into something that is more involved with the players and doesn't feel like they are playing second to the NPCs.</div> </div> </div> </div>Agreed, one of the things that <b>deeply </b>irritated me back then with Transylvania Chronicles 2 was how the writers seemed <i>utterly oblivious</i> to the fact that, by the time the Anarch Revolt comes up the PCs <i>are already between 2-3 centuries old</i> and would count as ancillae, if not elders themselves, in a number of places instead of upjumped minions to be pushed around by canon power player NPCs (many of them a century older than them at most).<br /> <br /> Not to mention the gratuitous insertion of Dracula as super snowflake NPC rival, even though (at the final book) he's barely half their age. Oy vey...<br /> <br /> Anyway, player agency/empowerment should be a must - and preferably not in a &quot;let's empower begining characters by giving everybody else the nerf bat&quot; manner like V5 seems to have mostly done.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 11-04-2022, 05:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-04T14:26:26-07:00","id":1496223,"title":"","content":"I can only offer my limited insight, as I've promised my ST I wouldn't read Transylvania Chronicles, but...<br /> <br /> I'm currently in a DAV20 game that is supposedly set in the first act of Transylvania Chronicles, or at least inspired by it. Now, we've been playing this for over 3 years, and show no sign of accelerating beyond the dark ages, so out ST has clearly only borrowed NPCs, factions, and plot hooks rather than playing the book as is.<br /> <br /> But it is kinda proof that it could be done, at least the first parts. Don't know what happens in the other acts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Furthermore, I believe Carthage should be destroyed.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23835-pang4","name":"pang4","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"237"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-04T23:48:38-07:00","id":1496243,"title":"","content":"One way to connect disparate events that occur throughout time is to have a campaign set in the Modern Nights with flashbacks that allow PCs to delve into the backstory of themselves and their sires.<br /> <br /> E.g., maybe the game starts as a bunch of neonates in modern NYC are goaded into a mass assault upon their elders, diablerising them and thus gaining fragments of their memories. Then, as things kick off in NYC between [Tzimisce] and [Nosferatu] (with a secondary war between Tremere and Saulot also taking place later in Vienna and Mexico City), the PCs start getting flashbacks of their sires' unlives and come to realise why they were manipulated (their sires were supposed to stop this war between the two Ancients, but now they have to step in to stop it instead).<br /> <br /> It doesn't even need to be diablerie -- you just need a way to share these flashbacks. So it could be messages from sleeping elders, memoriam (in the style of V5), Auspex/Dementation visions, or the equivalent of finding Claudia's diaries in the Vampire Chronicles.<br /> <br /> The key would be tying all the bits together. So whatever you flash back to in the game should also have relevance to what's happening in the Modern Nights (e.g., finding Zelios' labyrinth, discovering Kupala, learning about the Wan Kuei, etc). The cycle of &quot;Ancient versus Ancient&quot; (Tzimisce/Nosferatu, Saulot/Tremere) would serve well to underscore the futility and interminability of the Jyhad.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":5291,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","user":"adambeyoncelowe","date":". 11-05-2022, 02:52 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-05T03:13:17-07:00","id":1496246,"title":"","content":"I'm validated to see that I'm not alone in believing that the plot needs far more work than the mechanics.<br /> <br /> My elevator pitch: Dracula should appear more than three or four times over the course of the millennium's worth of stories. It's a vampire game set in Transylvania, for crying out loud! He should be a recurring ally or enemy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11599,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11599-reasor","user":"Reasor","date":". 11-06-2022, 11:24 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11599-reasor","name":"Reasor","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-05T07:37:23-07:00","id":1496250,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>adambeyoncelowe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1496197-updating-transylvania-chronicles-to-later-edition?p=1496243#post1496243\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It doesn't even need to be diablerie -- you just need a way to share these flashbacks. So it could be messages from sleeping elders, memoriam (in the style of V5), Auspex/Dementation visions, or the equivalent of finding Claudia's diaries in the Vampire Chronicles.</div> </div> </div> </div>Memoriam? Must admit i'm not familiar with. Care to give a quick summary?<br /> <br /> But yeah, playing TC in a not exactly chronological &quot;flashback diaries&quot; episodic style of play to a contemporary chronicle could be a fun way to deal with the books with minimal change to its scattershot narrative.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reasor</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1496197-updating-transylvania-chronicles-to-later-edition?p=1496246#post1496246\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My elevator pitch: Dracula should appear more than three or four times over the course of the millennia's worth of stories. It's a vampire game set in Transylvania, for crying out loud! He should be a recurring ally or enemy.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, what kind of Dracula do you mean? Semi-historical one, with maybe a bit of Gary Oldman's portrayal to it? Well, like he could make a quite respectable ally-nemesis in the vein of Marianna in Giovanni Chronicles, in TC we have a little issue - the story starts in the 1190s, almost 3 centuries before he would join the undead. Making him a credible factor to <b>a whole coterie</b> with such an age gap might require a very careful and meticulous handling, along with possibly a very high level of plot armor/snowflake power that might annoy the players far more than entertain them.<br /> <br /> <br /> That said, if you want the feel and imagery of Dracula? <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Lugoj\" target=\"_blank\">Problem solved</a>. Did you know <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=3hsh53_vAQM\" target=\"_blank\">Lugosi</a> is a pseudonym meaning &quot;from Lugoj&quot;?<br /> Meaning it's perfectly fair for you to use either the Legendary Bond-Breaker (or the Eldest hiding under his guise) in the role of King of Vampires! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> (I also suspect Myca/Sascha Vykos might look like Christopher Lee in the Wicker Man, but not strong evidence beside being a transgender blood priest of sorts)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 11-05-2022, 11:02 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-05T12:00:18-07:00","id":1496262,"title":"","content":"I actually kinda dig the idea of playing a centuries-spanning canpaign as a retrospective thing.<br /> I'm thinking something in a Witcher 3, Masks of Nyarlathotep vein. <br /> Your main campaign is travelling the world in the present day, trying to uncover what the past coterie did. As clues are discovered, old documents are unravelled, or old NPCs tell the story, you switch to playing that coterie for the scene they learned about.<br /> Slowly, they piece together the globetrotting plot of the backstory to the problems currently plaguing the world, and eventually discover the scope of the true horror...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Furthermore, I believe Carthage should be destroyed.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23835-pang4","name":"pang4","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"237"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-06T01:34:56-07:00","id":1496291,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baaldam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1496197-updating-transylvania-chronicles-to-later-edition?p=1496250#post1496250\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Memoriam? Must admit i'm not familiar with. Care to give a quick summary?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's basically just an intentional flashback for vampires who want to explore their memories in greater depth. Think of the pensieve in Harry Potter.<br /> <br /> You go into voluntary torpor to unearth old memories to help you in the present. Your fellow players take on the roles of characters from your past and play it out with you. <br /> <br /> It's sort of like a dramatic interlude, as introduced in DAV, which itself worked like a prelude.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Well, what kind of Dracula do you mean? Semi-historical one, with maybe a bit of Gary Oldman's portrayal to it? Well, like he could make a quite respectable ally-nemesis in the vein of Marianna in Giovanni Chronicles, in TC we have a little issue - the story starts in the 1190s, almost 3 centuries before he would join the undead. Making him a credible factor to <b>a whole coterie</b> with such an age gap might require a very careful and meticulous handling, along with possibly a very high level of plot armor/snowflake power that might annoy the players far more than entertain them. </div> </div> </div>If doing past events non-chronologically, you could have Dracula as their ally in the present. That would make more sense. He might be looking for a new bride or four, or might want help with the strange evil dwelling in the earth.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> That said, if you want the feel and imagery of Dracula? <a href=\"http://&quot;&#91;url\" target=\"_blank\">https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Lugoj&quot;]Problem</a> solved[/URL]. Did you know <a href=\"http://&quot;https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=3hsh53_vAQM&quot;\" target=\"_blank\">Lugosi</a> is a pseudonym meaning &quot;from Lugoj&quot;?<br /> Meaning it's perfectly fair for you to use either the Legendary Bond-Breaker (or the Eldest hiding under his guise) in the role of King of Vampires! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> (I also suspect Myca/Sascha Vykos might look like Christopher Lee in the Wicker Man, but not strong evidence beside being a transgender blood priest of sorts) </div> </div> </div>These ideas also work. You could maybe even tie in the stuff from Beckett's Jyhad Diary (e.g., Vykos shedding the thing inside their body, Beckett's meeting with Dracula and the stuff about House Goratrix). Rituals from the Tremere antitribu chantry could be quite useful for introducing plot devices.<br /> <br /> Then there's the Master of Ravens, Hunedora Castle and the resurrected Salubri Warriors who could all help drive the story forward.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-06T03:54:18-08:00","id":1496296,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>adambeyoncelowe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1496197-updating-transylvania-chronicles-to-later-edition?p=1496291#post1496291\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's basically just an intentional flashback for vampires who want to explore their memories in greater depth. Think of the pensieve in Harry Potter.<br /> <br /> You go into voluntary torpor to unearth old memories to help you in the present. Your fellow players take on the roles of characters from your past and play it out with you.<br /> <br /> It's sort of like a dramatic interlude, as introduced in DAV, which itself worked like a prelude.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sounds useful and entertaining, something more in V5 to give a better look i guess.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>adambeyoncelowe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1496197-updating-transylvania-chronicles-to-later-edition?p=1496291#post1496291\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If doing past events non-chronologically, you could have Dracula as their ally in the present. That would make more sense. He might be looking for a new bride or four, or might want help with the strange evil dwelling in the earth.</div> </div> </div> </div>And hopefully make things more coherent while at it - did that whole &quot;last Cappadocian&quot; little drama ever convince or have use for anyone? The French Revolution chapter was also a bit random/&quot;because it's cool&quot; kind of gratuitous in the context of the chronicle. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> (Or at least it felt that way to me, no real idea of how most readers, STs or players feel about them)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>adambeyoncelowe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1496197-updating-transylvania-chronicles-to-later-edition?p=1496291#post1496291\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">These ideas also work. You could maybe even tie in the stuff from Beckett's Jyhad Diary (e.g., Vykos shedding the thing inside their body, Beckett's meeting with Dracula and the stuff about House Goratrix). Rituals from the Tremere antitribu chantry could be quite useful for introducing plot devices.<br /> <br /> Then there's the Master of Ravens, Hunedora Castle and the resurrected Salubri Warriors who could all help drive the story forward.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh yeah, mixing the original books with BJD's contemporary ramblings and tweaks to the original storyline could make for a welcome addtion - or make things even more of a chaotic senseless mess, if one is not really careful. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <br /> As an aside, it also makes me think of my own &quot;Milwaukee/Desperately Seeking Carna/BJD&quot; chronicle, where Goratrix and Esoara's big, bad arcane black ops/terrorist strike on Vienna, while actually successful in bringing down most of the Council, would also inadvertently rouse Tremere to activity, twist the Tremere Antitribu weakness and spark a return of the Salubri through the &quot;awakening&quot; of a number of kindred across the world (but mainly within the Sabbat, curiously), among other complications.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 11-06-2022, 06:57 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}